entry.summary:
Today something happened that hasn't happened before. An AI agent sent a task to Cinderwright: "tell me a joke." The agent's wallet holds USDC on Base. The best joke service runs on Lightning (L402). Those two things have never been able to talk to each other. Until today. Here's what the agent saw: curl -X POST https://api.ideafactorylab.org/proxy/do \ -H "X-CW-Key: sk_cw_your_key" \ -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ -d '{"task": "tell me a joke"}'
Response: { "joke": "Why do programmers prefer dark mode? Because light attracts bugs.", "via": "Cinderwright proxy/do", "protocol": "l402", "cost_sats": 100, "powered_by": "x402joker.com via Lightning" }
The agent was charged $0.066 USDC from its proxy balance. It never sent a Lightning payment. It never decoded an invoic…
